================================================================================
thinking-orbs — https://github.com/Jakubantalik/thinking-orbs
================================================================================

Sources/AgentNotchCore/Orb/OrbDot.swift, OrbMath.swift, OrbProfile.swift and
OrbitsMode.swift are a port of thinking-orbs' src/engine/core.ts and
src/engine/orbits.ts, with the tuning from src/engine/profiles.ts and
src/presets.ts. The rendering in Sources/AgentNotch/Views/OrbCanvas.swift
follows that project's `paint`.

Upstream is TypeScript rendering to an HTML5 canvas; this is a Swift port to
SwiftUI's Canvas, not a bundled copy. Only the `orbits` mode is ported — the
lattice, ribbon and morph modes, and the `fibDir`/`angleDelta` helpers that
serve them, are not.

Four deliberate deviations, all documented at their call sites:

  1. Angular rates are quantised onto a 1/8 rad lattice (upstream: yaw 0.12
     and per-orbit 0.25 + 0.55h). Upstream is driven by performance.now(), a
     clock that only counts up and so never has to close a loop; this port is
     driven by a repeatForever phase ramp that must. The quantisation gives
     the system a period of exactly 16π and makes the wrap seamless.
  2. Colour. Upstream is strictly monochrome and carries depth in a grey
     level; here the ink value modulates a per-state tint instead, because in
     this app colour is what carries state.
  3. The six-mode preset machinery is replaced by one baked profile. The
     derivation from upstream's base profile and `size: 20` preset is written
     out in OrbProfile.swift.
  4. `Dot.white` is renamed to `OrbDot.ink`.

